{
  "title": "Cathedral",
  "about": "A gothic nave you fly down and never reach the end of: clustered piers, pointed arcades onto dark aisles, a rib vault overhead, and above the arcade a great window in every bay whose tracery is the fractal, arches inside arches inside arches. Light is the subject: a rose window burns at the far end and throws beams back down the nave, sun shafts slant through the glass and pool on the floor, and the stone stands dark against the glowing haze. The kick lurches you forward and flares the light, the hats make the glass glitter, the chords turn its colours, and the glass follows the show hue; if the projector struggles, lower Steps.",
  "groups": [
    {"name": "Structure", "params": [
      {"id": "sides", "label": "Rose window petals", "min": 4, "max": 16, "step": 1, "default": 8},
      {"id": "detail", "label": "Tracery generations (detail)", "min": 2, "max": 5, "step": 1, "default": 3},
      {"id": "scale", "label": "Tracery: next arches smaller by", "min": 1.3, "max": 2.4, "step": 0.01, "default": 1.3},
      {"id": "form", "label": "Tracery: oculus size", "min": 0.2, "max": 1.6, "step": 0.01, "default": 1.0},
      {"id": "fold", "label": "Tracery: foils (plain to cusped)", "min": 0, "max": 1, "step": 0.005, "default": 0.6},
